# 6541364.isf

Dataset: seis-radius — Great earthquakes in the ISC bulletin: nine named ones (Rayleigh arrivals
  for the radius, P / first arrivals for our relocation, the P shadow zone) and every shallow Mw >=
  7.0 of 2000-2023 for the pooled syntheses
File: data/seis/bulk/raw/6541364.isf
SHA-256: 9d30276521bd49f541da93656edc2e885f1a00d17867f1da2fccb13c359b3dd0 (also in
  data/seis/inputs.lock; check with: cd data/seis && sha256sum -c inputs.lock)
In the public repository: no, only this description and the hash: the file may be shared but is kept
  out of git for its size. Get it from fog fetch seis-radius, then compare its SHA-256 with the one
  above.
Obtained: the answer of a public web API to the request given.
From: ISC On-line Bulletin, ISF2 of each earthquake of the catalogue query, fetched one by one.
Collected: 2026-09-19
Licence: other — ISC On-line Bulletin: free with the citation International Seismological Centre,
  On-line Bulletin, https://doi.org/10.31905/D808B830. Natural Earth: public domain.
Sources:
- International Seismological Centre, On-line Bulletin (ISF2 phase data)
  <https://doi.org/10.31905/D808B830>
- Natural Earth, 1:50m land polygons (ne_50m_land), public domain
  <https://www.naturalearthdata.com/>
Evidence class (rule 10): check
Where the Earth's radius enters:
- distance_deg: angles from the published epicentre and station coordinates, then the surface-wave
  speeds the tab uses were established with distances measured on the globe
- ocean_frac: Natural Earth land polygons, drawn in degrees on the globe
What would vindicate the flat model (rule 5): A reconstructed radius 60-100% off, the error a flat
  map's distances would need; the real arrivals land within a few percent. Pooled: one flat map,
  with the same free parameters, fitting the pooled P times or the pooled shadow as well as the
  globe.
Built by: fog build seis-radius, fog build seis-relocate, fog build seis-shadow, fog build
  seis-bulk, fog build seis-mesh
