Notes: Edit events.json only (one entry per earthquake), then fog fetch seis-radius (ISC query;
  Natural Earth once), fog lock seis-radius, fog build seis-radius. Until 2026-10-14 the land
  polygons were downloaded afresh at every run, from the branch head; they are now an input with a
  hash. The same bulletins feed fog build seis-relocate: earthquakes relocated from arrival times
  and station angles only (epic18). The pooled syntheses (fog build seis-bulk, 2026-10-29) use every
  earthquake the ISC catalogue query of tools/internal/build/seisbulk/fetch.go returns: reviewed ISC
  Bulletin, 2000-01-01 to 2023-12-31, depth <= 70 km, GCMT Mw >= 7.0 (264 events), then at least 50
  P stations 25-95 degrees from our own centre; bulletins by event id in bulk/raw/ (gitignored, fog
  fetch seis-radius). The nine named earthquakes that meet the rule are counted there again,
  processed like the others.

Written by `fog build explain` from data/seis/dataset.json and data/seis/inputs.lock: edit those, not this file.
